    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n21132" root="سوأ" body-key="s">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">خَزْيَانُ سَوْآنُ</span></b>  is [app. an instance of the alteration of the latter of two epithets to assimilate it to
the former, originally <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">خَزْيَانُ أَسْوَأُ</span>, meaning
<i>Ashamed,</i> or <i>base,</i> or <i>vile,</i> or <i>ignominious,</i> and
<i>evil, bad,</i> &amp;c.,] from <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">القُبْحُ</span>. (M, TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  See also
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سَوْءَةٌ</span>.

